📘 Kubernetes & OpenShift CLI and API – Quick Summary
1️⃣ Ways to Manage an OpenShift Cluster
You can manage a Red Hat OpenShift Container Platform (RHOCP) cluster using:
Web Console
A graphical interface in the browser used for:
•	Deploying applications
•	Viewing cluster health
•	Monitoring resources
•	Viewing logs and metrics
Command Line Interfaces (CLI)
Two main tools:
CLI	Purpose
kubectl	Standard Kubernetes CLI
oc	OpenShift CLI (superset of kubectl)
Example:
oc get pods
kubectl get pods
oc provides additional OpenShift features.
________________________________________
2️⃣ Getting Help for CLI Commands
Every command supports --help.
Example:
oc get --help
This shows:
•	command syntax
•	options
•	examples
________________________________________
3️⃣ Projects (Namespaces)
A project in OpenShift is the same as a Kubernetes namespace.
Purpose:
•	isolate applications
•	separate environments
•	control access
Example:
oc new-project myapp
Projects allow:
•	multi-tenant clusters
•	resource separation
________________________________________
4️⃣ Authentication in OpenShift
OpenShift supports several login methods.
Most reliable method:
Token authentication
Example:
oc login --token=<token> --server=<cluster-url>
Reason:
Enterprise systems may replace the web console login page with SSO.
________________________________________
5️⃣ API Resources
All Kubernetes and OpenShift objects are API resources.
Examples:
•	Pods
•	Services
•	Nodes
•	ConfigMaps
•	Deployments
Admin tasks usually involve:
•	creating resources
•	viewing resources
•	modifying resources
Example:
oc get pods
oc create -f pod.yaml
oc delete pod mypod
________________________________________
6️⃣ YAML and JSON Output
CLI commands can output data in structured formats.
Formats:
Format	Use
YAML	configuration files
JSON	scripting & automation
Examples:
oc get pod mypod -o yaml
oc get pod mypod -o json
These formats help with:
•	automation
•	scripting
•	debugging
________________________________________
7️⃣ Operators in OpenShift
Operators automate application lifecycle management.
Operators can:
•	install applications
•	perform health checks
•	monitor workloads
•	handle upgrades
•	maintain desired state
Example operator resources:
oc get clusteroperators
Operators are central to OpenShift automation.
________________________________________
8️⃣ Monitoring in OpenShift
OpenShift includes a built-in monitoring stack.
Based on:
Prometheus
Features:
•	metrics collection
•	alerts
•	cluster health monitoring
Components include:
•	Prometheus
•	Alertmanager
•	Grafana-style dashboards
________________________________________
9️⃣ Monitoring in Web Console
The OpenShift web console provides:
•	cluster usage graphs
•	CPU and memory metrics
•	pod statistics
•	resource utilization
It also allows:
•	running Prometheus queries
•	configuring alerts
•	visualizing metrics
________________________________________
🔟 Logs for Troubleshooting
OpenShift allows viewing logs from:
•	containers
•	pods
Example:
oc logs mypod
Logs help diagnose:
•	application failures
•	startup problems
•	configuration errors
________________________________________
1️⃣1️⃣ Collecting Cluster Debug Data
OpenShift provides a command to collect cluster diagnostics.
Command:
oc adm must-gather
This gathers:
•	cluster configurations
•	resource definitions
•	logs
•	events
It is commonly used when:
•	opening Red Hat support cases
•	debugging cluster issues
Example:
oc adm must-gather --dest-dir ./debug
________________________________________
⭐ Key Commands to Remember
Command	Purpose
oc login	login to cluster
oc get	view resources
oc describe	detailed resource info
oc logs	view container logs
oc api-resources	list resource types
oc version	cluster version
oc adm top	resource usage
oc adm must-gather	cluster debugging
________________________________________
🧠 Key Concepts to Remember
•	OpenShift can be managed using Web Console or CLI
•	Projects isolate resources
•	Operators manage applications automatically
•	Prometheus monitors cluster health
•	YAML/JSON outputs enable automation
•	Logs and must-gather help with troubleshooting

